WEBVTT

00:16.460 --> 00:19.360
If my eyes are blinded by the sun

00:19.360 --> 00:24.040
I may just see the limits of the light.

00:24.040 --> 00:25.940
The mind of stardust

00:25.940 --> 00:31.780
What a small universe I live in

00:31.780 --> 00:39.320
Won't somebody give me
a code that starts at zero?

00:39.320 --> 00:41.890
Multiplied and in confusion

00:41.890 --> 00:45.920
A colony dead inside its cage

00:45.920 --> 00:50.400
Shoot your cowardly dreams

00:50.400 --> 00:53.570
Loneliness... self-destruct!

00:53.570 --> 00:57.970
No matter what sacrifices we make

00:57.970 --> 01:01.810
for a future just beyond reach

01:01.810 --> 01:05.480
Let our hearts speak to each other

01:05.480 --> 01:08.780
deep down inside

01:08.780 --> 01:12.920
Though the days just one step behind

01:12.920 --> 01:15.920
will pass even farther from us

01:15.920 --> 01:22.990
You will be in my thoughts

01:42.680 --> 01:45.310
There are two kinds of power.

01:48.490 --> 01:50.360
Power that should be used...

01:50.360 --> 01:52.690
and power that shouldn't be.

01:53.960 --> 01:57.730
Generally I prefer to avoid
scrapping it out like this, but...

01:59.360 --> 02:01.560
Put away your weapons!

02:06.170 --> 02:09.210
Now that the Destruct Code is no longer here...

02:09.210 --> 02:14.710
fighting the Salvation Committee
serves no useful purpose whatsoever.

02:14.710 --> 02:19.080
Cease all violence at once.
Cease all violence at once.

02:23.390 --> 02:25.390
I should've known...

02:25.390 --> 02:28.990
The guys you've got here still
can't do squat if ain't by the book.

02:34.330 --> 02:38.560
What a damn hassle, just to
meet up with an old acquaintance.

02:40.240 --> 02:43.580
So it's you.

02:43.580 --> 02:45.340
The Eagle Master?!

02:51.250 --> 02:56.210
"There are Two Kinds of Power"

02:57.890 --> 03:00.290
Been a while, hasn't it?

03:00.290 --> 03:03.060
I reckon the last time we saw each other...

03:03.060 --> 03:06.300
was after the Elephant Master
went soft and left us flapping in the wind.

03:06.300 --> 03:09.600
If the head of the Salvation
Committee is making appearances in person...

03:09.600 --> 03:13.640
then things must be really desperate for you.

03:13.640 --> 03:18.440
I just don't take to sitting in
front of a desk like you, that's all.

03:18.440 --> 03:22.210
I take it you've come for the Destruct Code.

03:22.210 --> 03:24.650
What else is there?

03:24.650 --> 03:25.980
But...

03:25.980 --> 03:29.450
From the look of things, I'd say you
let it slip right through your fingers.

03:29.450 --> 03:32.660
So where'd those Destruction
Committee morons head off to?

03:32.660 --> 03:36.420
If I knew that, I wouldn't be standing
around here with my thumb up my butt.

03:39.460 --> 03:41.130
Fair enough.

03:41.130 --> 03:43.500
Search the area around
town with a fine-toothed comb!

03:43.500 --> 03:45.970
They can't have gotten far!

03:45.970 --> 03:47.060
Yessir!

03:48.670 --> 03:50.660
Sorry to disturb.

03:54.850 --> 03:57.420
Lia...

03:57.420 --> 04:01.920
You've spent all this time and you
still haven't accomplished your objective.

04:01.920 --> 04:06.690
I was counting on your Dragon blood
and the matchless power of your tribe...

04:06.690 --> 04:09.090
but was that foolish?

04:09.090 --> 04:11.160
I have no excuse.

04:11.160 --> 04:14.100
The same goes for you, Nadja.

04:14.100 --> 04:18.670
I once thought very highly
of that intellect of yours...

04:18.670 --> 04:19.700
But now, well...

04:19.700 --> 04:24.840
Perhaps this is all we can expect from a
human-beastman halfbreed like yourself.

04:24.840 --> 04:27.050
I'm afraid I also have no excuse.

04:27.050 --> 04:30.150
For the time being, you two
nincompoops are to wait here.

04:30.150 --> 04:34.450
And as for the
Destruct Code, I'll go get it myself!

04:51.640 --> 04:53.740
Nadja...

04:53.740 --> 04:56.740
What now? What do you plan to do?

04:56.740 --> 04:58.480
What are you getting at?

04:58.480 --> 05:01.850
Those things he said to us...
I have no intention of taking it lying down!

05:01.850 --> 05:03.350
It's been like this all along...

05:03.350 --> 05:06.180
but we don't have to just blindly
take orders from that Eagle Master!

05:06.180 --> 05:08.890
And wait around here like idiots!

05:08.890 --> 05:13.520
We can just go after the Destruction
Committee by ourselves, can't we?!

05:18.430 --> 05:21.200
Yeah, about that... Lia...

05:21.200 --> 05:22.670
Those three...

05:22.670 --> 05:27.170
Do you think they're
honestly out to destroy the world?

05:27.170 --> 05:29.570
What's this, all of a sudden?!

05:29.570 --> 05:32.010
Of course they are.

05:32.010 --> 05:34.450
Well, I have my doubts.

05:34.450 --> 05:36.580
The whole time we've been chasing them...

05:36.580 --> 05:42.620
time and again, they do things that seem
pretty far removed from world destruction.

05:42.620 --> 05:44.850
Time... and time again.

06:06.710 --> 06:08.880
I have a hard time understanding it.

06:08.880 --> 06:12.040
I mean, why are they doing this?

06:12.780 --> 06:15.050
Why are you brooding like this?!

06:15.050 --> 06:18.990
They're the World Destruction
Committee, and that's all there is to it!

06:18.990 --> 06:19.960
And especially!

06:19.960 --> 06:23.620
The one I really can't stand is that woman!

06:25.130 --> 06:32.470
Like you said, maybe they have done
things that don't jibe with world destruction.

06:32.470 --> 06:33.500
But still!

06:33.500 --> 06:35.470
That woman!

06:40.410 --> 06:45.510
That woman is dead meat!
I'll capture her if it's the last thing I do...!

06:46.450 --> 06:49.420
H-Hey! Wait up!

06:49.420 --> 06:52.120
So then, what's my next move?

06:52.120 --> 06:54.830
Despite my huge investment
in all those clockwork robots...

06:54.830 --> 06:57.200
they still couldn't keep up with those three.

06:57.200 --> 07:00.690
They're turning out to be a
much tougher quarry than I thought.

07:09.040 --> 07:11.110
Dragon Valley...

07:11.110 --> 07:17.150
That scene of Dragon Valley
that the Destruct Code showed us...

07:17.150 --> 07:20.640
So that's it! Now it all makes sense.

07:22.120 --> 07:26.650
Now that you mention it, your home
wasn't too far away from here, was it?

07:27.890 --> 07:28.890
That's right.

07:28.890 --> 07:32.730
Over there, on the other side of
the desert... you can just make it out.

07:32.730 --> 07:36.570
That's where I'm from... the winter continent.

07:36.570 --> 07:40.030
Although I haven't been back
there in a hundred years or more.

07:42.510 --> 07:44.480
A hundred years?

07:44.480 --> 07:45.580
Lia...

07:45.580 --> 07:50.180
I'm well aware that this may be an
extremely rude question for a lady, but...

07:50.180 --> 07:52.920
What is it? Why are you acting so formal?

07:52.920 --> 07:56.090
How... old are you?

07:56.090 --> 07:58.920
I think I must be over
300 or so years old by now.

07:58.920 --> 08:01.560
I don't really keep count.

08:01.560 --> 08:04.160
Three... hundred?!

08:04.160 --> 08:09.670
I know what you're getting at...
you thought I was older, didn't you?

08:09.670 --> 08:12.570
Maybe it's because I look so ladylike?

08:12.570 --> 08:17.940
Well, that's not exactly... oh, never mind.

08:17.940 --> 08:22.010
Lia, you haven't been with the
Salvation Committee for long, have you?

08:22.010 --> 08:23.280
No.

08:23.280 --> 08:26.120
Well, you've been alive this whole 300 years...

08:26.120 --> 08:30.050
so what made you suddenly
decide to join the Salvation Committee?

08:30.050 --> 08:33.730
They say if the
Destruct Code unleashes its power...

08:33.730 --> 08:38.630
then everything both living and
dead will revert back to elemental sand.

08:38.630 --> 08:41.600
That means both me and the place I come from.

08:41.600 --> 08:46.240
I can't just sit quiet and
let something like that happen!

08:46.240 --> 08:50.380
I see. It's simplistic, like you.

08:50.380 --> 08:53.040
The things you say! Well, what about you?

08:53.040 --> 08:57.580
I value my life, too. But I have
another reason for doing this.

08:57.580 --> 09:00.490
The Salvation Committee is an
organization where ability is rewarded.

09:00.490 --> 09:03.150
And since I have all the
qualities it takes to rise to the top...

09:03.150 --> 09:05.460
there's no way I wouldn't join.

09:05.460 --> 09:07.260
Your reason is just as simplistic as mine.

09:07.260 --> 09:10.090
That's right... the result
of a simple calculation.

09:12.460 --> 09:17.330
But when it comes to those three,
the reasoning seems a bit more complicated.

09:22.110 --> 09:26.240
So then... should we chase after them or not?

09:29.580 --> 09:34.120
So I hear your home isn't
too far from here, isn't that so?

09:34.120 --> 09:37.090
And what business is that of yours?

09:37.090 --> 09:41.590
Yeah well, it's just that something
keeps nagging at the back of my mind.

09:41.590 --> 09:46.830
Your home of Dragon Valley is
surrounded by snow and steep, craggy cliffs...

09:46.830 --> 09:50.840
and they say anyone who's not of
the Dragon tribe is promptly turned away.

09:50.840 --> 09:56.770
But if the visitor is the Destruct Code
itself, who knows what might happen.

09:56.770 --> 09:58.640
What are you getting at?!

09:58.640 --> 10:04.780
You saw it, didn't you? When the
Destruct Code showed us that place.

10:04.780 --> 10:11.520
Most likely they came here
because the Destruct Code led them here.

10:11.520 --> 10:13.220
Which means...

10:13.220 --> 10:14.690
You can't mean!

10:14.690 --> 10:18.830
I think you'd better move quickly on this.

10:18.830 --> 10:22.670
You don't want your
precious home destroyed, do you?

10:22.670 --> 10:24.830
That woman!

10:31.040 --> 10:33.200
She really is simplistic.

10:38.520 --> 10:42.690
So... you say you're heading
for the winter continent now?

10:42.690 --> 10:43.880
Yes.

10:45.020 --> 10:49.530
This thing reacted much more
strongly than it ever has before.

10:49.530 --> 10:54.520
I have a feeling we might be
nearing the end of our journey.

11:00.070 --> 11:05.530
Well, as long as I'm getting paid,
I'll take you wherever you wanna go.

11:07.910 --> 11:09.050
What's this?

11:09.050 --> 11:13.780
You haven't forgotten the trouble you
had on the summer continent, have you?

11:13.780 --> 11:17.380
You really thought you could show up
at the winter continent in those clothes?

11:17.860 --> 11:21.060
So? How much extra are
those gonna cost us, bear-o?

11:21.060 --> 11:25.120
Ah, I see you've grown
accustomed to doing business with me!

11:55.760 --> 11:58.260
Have you seen my companion?

11:58.260 --> 12:00.290
She's from the Dragon tribe.

12:02.070 --> 12:03.400
What's the problem?

12:03.400 --> 12:08.110
You have been identified as
half human and half beastman.

12:08.110 --> 12:11.340
I cannot determine whether I am
allowed to answer your question or not.

12:11.340 --> 12:13.780
I see...

12:13.780 --> 12:15.680
Well, let's do it this way...

12:15.680 --> 12:20.080
I'll be fine with vague information
that only half answers my question...

12:20.080 --> 12:22.350
so try answering me like that.

12:24.360 --> 12:26.620
As... you... wish.

12:26.620 --> 12:29.990
Have you seen my companion?

12:29.990 --> 12:32.830
I may have seen her... or maybe not.

12:32.830 --> 12:37.030
She may have seemed to be
heading somewhere... or maybe not.

12:37.030 --> 12:39.800
Where was she heading?

12:39.800 --> 12:45.040
She may have seemed to be heading
for the winter continent... or maybe not.

12:45.040 --> 12:47.980
In that case, where did the Alligator Master go?

12:47.980 --> 12:51.350
Our Alligator Master may be
chasing the Destruction Committee...

12:51.350 --> 12:56.320
and he may have set the Dragon
female out after them... or maybe not.

12:56.320 --> 12:59.780
I understand. That'll be all.

13:21.550 --> 13:24.320
Hey, Penguin.

13:24.320 --> 13:26.680
What's on your mind, Walrus?

13:26.680 --> 13:28.220
What are all these footprints?

13:28.220 --> 13:31.190
Oh, just some travelers.

13:31.190 --> 13:37.220
A couple o' humans and one beastman...
a strange combo if I've ever seen one.

13:40.030 --> 13:43.570
They're not... headin' for
Dragon Valley, are they?!

13:43.570 --> 13:48.940
I tried to stop 'em, but they
wouldn't listen... kept sayin' they had to.

13:50.110 --> 13:55.410
Well, I sure hope they turn back...
before they run afoul of that Dragon tribe.

13:57.880 --> 14:00.220
About those travelers...

14:00.220 --> 14:03.380
You're going to tell me all about them!

14:07.190 --> 14:09.130
Morte...

14:09.130 --> 14:11.960
Let's just... take a small break...

14:11.960 --> 14:16.770
Stop being stupid! If we stop now,
we'll be blocks of ice in no time flat!

14:16.770 --> 14:21.210
But I mean, we don't even
know if we're going the right way!

14:21.210 --> 14:24.240
That penguin told us
this was the way, didn't he?

14:24.240 --> 14:27.880
That doesn't mean we have to run out
and climb up some snow-covered mountain!

14:27.880 --> 14:30.050
Not just on one guy's say-so!

14:30.050 --> 14:32.880
C'mon, Toppy, back me up!

14:43.630 --> 14:48.830
Toppy, please tell me you aren't about
to start hibernating on us or anything...

14:48.830 --> 14:50.330
What're you talking about, bear-o?!

14:50.330 --> 14:52.800
It's not like I'm some bear,
so how could I possibly do that, bear-o?!

14:52.800 --> 14:56.830
I'm going right now, bear-o!
Of all the crazy things!

14:57.780 --> 15:03.770
I wonder why he has such a thing
about not wanting to admit he's a bear...

15:36.310 --> 15:40.040
It kinda seems like a graveyard, doesn't it?

15:45.320 --> 15:47.960
I think I've seen one of these before...

15:47.960 --> 15:49.320
Stop right there!

15:50.730 --> 15:55.630
This is our Dragon tribe's hallowed ground!

15:55.630 --> 15:58.740
What do you think you're trying to do here?!

15:58.740 --> 16:01.740
Hard to say. Why don't
you figure it out for yourself?

16:01.740 --> 16:04.410
H-H-Hold on! Morte, knock it off!

16:04.410 --> 16:06.640
If we make her mad, she can be really scary!

16:06.640 --> 16:09.510
Stop being so annoying...
don't you think it's a little late for that?

16:09.510 --> 16:14.080
I'm saying it's crazy!
Fighting in a place like this!

16:14.080 --> 16:19.020
And you... what do you
think you're doing, anyway?

16:19.020 --> 16:21.160
All that world destruction nonsense!

16:21.160 --> 16:22.590
If the world were destroyed...

16:22.590 --> 16:27.030
neither you nor your friends
could even be alive, you know!

16:27.030 --> 16:30.940
What about you?! You and
your ridiculous "world salvation"...

16:30.940 --> 16:33.440
You can't tell me you
honestly believe that crap!

16:33.440 --> 16:35.070
You call it ridiculous?!

16:35.070 --> 16:39.840
"Saving" a world where the only way
of life is beastmen ruling over humans...

16:39.840 --> 16:42.250
I'm saying it's beyond ridiculous.

16:42.250 --> 16:46.720
If you can't even see that,
then you really are stupid!

16:46.720 --> 16:52.090
Considering the way the world is,
this system of rulership is best for everyone.

16:52.090 --> 16:54.020
Just look back at histor...

16:59.130 --> 17:01.570
Morte, what've you done?!

17:01.570 --> 17:03.100
Shut up already!

17:03.100 --> 17:07.760
I just can't stand women who try to
push their values onto everyone els...

17:12.880 --> 17:17.110
I can see it was stupid of
me to try and reason with you.

17:17.110 --> 17:19.640
It would seem so.

17:22.290 --> 17:25.050
Go to hell!

17:27.730 --> 17:31.390
Ow-ow-ow-ow-ow-ow!

17:38.240 --> 17:41.410
You world destruction bitch...!

17:41.410 --> 17:43.670
A little brat like you...

17:43.670 --> 17:46.840
What would you know about it?!

17:49.310 --> 17:50.640
She did it?

17:54.750 --> 17:57.020
You called me a brat!

18:03.460 --> 18:08.330
Oh crap! Toppy, things aren't
looking so good! At this rate...

18:11.270 --> 18:14.640
Wake up! Wake up, Toppy!

18:16.040 --> 18:20.280
You keep feedin' me honey like
this... I'm gonna get fat, bear-o...

18:20.280 --> 18:23.770
Why're you... saying things...
in your sleep... that make sense, Toppy?!

18:32.560 --> 18:37.560
Destroying the world... have you ever
even thought about what that means?!

18:37.560 --> 18:40.700
People like you use force to
keep humans under your thumb!

18:40.700 --> 18:42.230
So you're the last
person I wanna hear that from!

18:42.230 --> 18:44.640
All your talk of "saving the world"...

18:44.640 --> 18:46.690
Stop being so glib and try
hearing what you're saying!

18:48.370 --> 18:50.140
Come on... come on...

18:51.840 --> 18:53.510
Oh, you're awake?!

18:53.510 --> 18:54.580
Toppy?

18:54.580 --> 18:57.180
There are two kinds of bears, bear-o.

18:57.180 --> 18:58.350
Huh?!

18:58.350 --> 19:00.750
Strongly omnivorous bears...

19:00.750 --> 19:03.720
and strongly carnivorous bears, bear-o.

19:03.720 --> 19:06.060
Bears who live out on the open snow...

19:06.060 --> 19:09.160
typically rely on seals for their
primary sustenance, which means...

19:09.160 --> 19:12.650
I don't need that kind of
information right now, Toppy!

19:34.520 --> 19:37.850
The game is up.

19:39.720 --> 19:41.420
Lia!

19:42.030 --> 19:44.090
Move away from there!

19:44.090 --> 19:46.930
Nadja, what are you doing here?!

19:54.740 --> 19:57.230
What was that sound, bear-o?

20:04.250 --> 20:05.620
The Alligator Master!

20:05.620 --> 20:06.880
Lia!

20:13.260 --> 20:17.420
The Alligator Master?! What's he up to?

20:22.830 --> 20:25.430
Lia!

20:40.520 --> 20:42.090
There it is.

20:42.090 --> 20:46.020
Head out... the Destruct Code's over that way!

20:51.300 --> 20:53.460
The Destruct Code!

20:56.030 --> 21:00.160
This is bad, bear-o! They're
after the Destruct Code, bear-o!

21:05.810 --> 21:08.840
We're gonna make it! We'll get there faster!

21:31.540 --> 21:35.900
What the...?! We're right on
the edge! Right on the edge!

21:39.240 --> 21:44.080
I swear, you three are
about as lucky as they come.

21:46.020 --> 21:54.480
But now that the Destruct Code
has become mine, your luck is at an end.

22:21.080 --> 22:24.590
The glimmering seas of sand

22:24.590 --> 22:27.720
The end of the green earth

22:27.720 --> 22:33.800
Memories overflowing from the sky

22:33.800 --> 22:36.930
now plunged into darkness

22:36.930 --> 22:40.140
The memories will pile up

22:40.140 --> 22:46.140
like mounds of rubble

22:46.140 --> 22:49.380
Mutual encounters

22:49.380 --> 22:52.450
Misunderstood feelings

22:52.450 --> 22:55.590
Interwoven words

22:55.590 --> 22:58.720
People hurting each other

22:58.720 --> 23:10.830
Does the path we walk on
still lead us to tomorrow?

23:13.670 --> 23:17.510
Living this moment against the world

23:17.510 --> 23:20.510
isn't just about changing the world

23:20.510 --> 23:26.080
We're off on a distant journey across the waves

23:26.080 --> 23:29.650
So let our living heartbeat echo in the wind

23:29.650 --> 23:33.190
Around the world, to the end of the world

23:33.190 --> 23:39.160
Until we reach

23:39.160 --> 23:50.770
the promised land just beyond

23:52.110 --> 23:54.380
We've been knocked down
to the bottom of a steep ravine.

23:54.380 --> 23:58.820
We try making our way through a
deep cave to recapture the Destruct Code...

23:58.820 --> 24:03.520
but unfortunately, all who step foot
inside are drawn into a dreamworld...

24:03.520 --> 24:05.060
the cave is a legendary labyrinth!

24:05.060 --> 24:07.490
I told you, boss... I'm wiping it down...

24:07.490 --> 24:09.690
What are you wiping down, bear-o?!

24:09.690 --> 24:12.660
Next time on World Destruction... Episode 12:

24:12.660 --> 24:14.200
"There Are Two Kinds of Pasts."

24:14.200 --> 24:16.570
Lotta sand... everywhere...

24:16.570 --> 24:18.240
Lotta strands of hair?!

24:18.240 --> 24:19.670
Morte, what are you...?!

24:19.670 --> 24:20.660
Bear-o!
